<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Thursday were forecast to see rain in the west, sun in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see cloudy skies with a chance of showers with highs of 18 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see rain in the southwest and north with highs of 22 to 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sunny skies with highs of 20 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
